{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfr6iZXsevNn9Jyh1WDkU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Grid.** Use 2×2-pixel cells, giving 80×100. At 4bpp one cell is exactly one video byte on two scanlines, so drawing needs no shifts or masks. Store one byte per cell in an 82×102 array (8,364 bytes) with a sentinel land border, which removes all bounds checks. Values are SEA, LAND, TRAIL, plus a MARK bit.\n\n**Enemies.** Keep parallel arrays: a cell offset (word) and a delta (signed word, ±1 ±82). Collision is one lookup, `grid[off+delta]`: LAND means bounce, TRAIL means the player dies. There are no pairwise tests; land-crawlers just compare their offset word against the player's.\n\n**Fill.** On trail closure, run a scanline span fill from each sea enemy's cell, skipping any already marked. Use `REP SCASB`/`REP STOSB` for spans and an explicit 1K-word seed stack. Then make one `LODSB`/`XLAT`/`STOSB` pass: unmarked SEA and TRAIL become LAND (redraw, increment the percent counter), and MARK clears. That is roughly 0.2s at 4.77MHz.\n\n**Memory.** About 11K total, plus the 16K framebuffer."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":3552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":630},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"09df7574-7757-4845-aa66-856d4b843ac0","uuid":"11f2372e-d2ca-4d03-8430-65c55bbeec1b","timestamp":"2026-10-09T05:19:46.084Z","request_id":"req_011Cfr6iZFWepb78MQrkK8oY"}
